From 86ef180a0dfad275a8a05a519e2e31c68cd7491c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Harzva <49864959+Harzva@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 15:19:24 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] codex: refresh managed model catalogs in secondary local
 homes

A desktop magpie started without CODEX_HOME refreshed only its primary
home. Already-connected secondary homes kept an old model_catalog_json
file, so a newly available model such as Qwen4 was absent in that
account's Codex picker even after magpie refreshed its providers.

Add catalog-only discovery of secondary homes, including bounded account
manager containers, without expanding credential or session discovery.
Update only existing managed catalogs still routed to this local gateway.
Retain each home's native entries, extra metadata and chosen effort;
leave config, sign-in, threads, profiles, custom/remote catalogs and
redirected or shared files alone. Reuse the existing entry generator,
ordering, list fitting and user-field preservation.

Verification on initial source base a3d2a85dd3803a3b8208d40fe5f61e8e63712e62:
- The final CatalogSync and ProviderCatalog tests fail with only the new
  SyncCatalog hook removed; they pass with it enabled.
- Go 1.26.8: 34 catalog/desktop/home tests pass, including independently
  added large-list, explicit-home, invalid-file and ownership cases.
- Go 1.27.2 / macOS SDK 27: native, Linux and Windows vet/build pass;
  focused race checks pass. gofmt and diff whitespace checks are clean.
- Real codex-cli 0.167.0-alpha.3.2 app-server model/list, using generated
  synthetic local catalogs: Qwen4 absent before sync, present afterwards.
  No model inference, real sign-in or installed-app update was performed.
- The full Go 1.27.2 nogui suite was run and is NOT clean. JSON-v2 and
  allocation failures pass on the required Go 1.26.8. Selected file-group,
  disclaimed-process and Library child checks pass with tiny runtime
  fixtures on ordinary internal APFS; builds and caches remain external.
  Other full-suite failures remain unclassified; no full-suite success
  is claimed. The submission records these limits for maintainer review.

Final validation after a clean rebase onto current main
bc59aefd096c0d11ea0a8bdd9ac47349030ec718:
- Go 1.26.8: the same 34 catalog/desktop/home tests pass. Native/Linux/
  Windows vet and builds and focused race checks all exit 0.
- Independent read-only review of the rebased nine-file diff found no
  blocking issue. Final generated fixtures were read again by the real
  Codex app-server with the same before/after result.
- No full-suite success is claimed after the rebase. Linux and Windows
  runtime checks and GUI browser tests were not run; GUI assets are
  unchanged. This is a source contribution for review, not a release.
